> Preserve the transfer example and every key-bit change

Use the original public key shared-secret-key and message transfer $100 to
Alice. Ordinary array equality demonstrates that recomputation agrees, while the
original changed payee/amount and guessed key disagree. This is a functional
equality example, not a constant-time verification API. A real message protocol
also needs an unambiguous encoding and its own replay handling; those behaviors
are outside this hash calculation. A MAC does not encrypt the message or
distinguish which holder of a shared key produced it.

The 17-byte key gives 136 single-bit changes. Bit j changes byte floor(j/8), bit
(j mod 8), least-significant bit first. For each complete changed key, the
native helper computes an actual tag and its exact Hamming distance from the
baseline. The full histogram has 257 bins for distances 0 through 256; no
observation is clamped into a convenient endpoint bin. Under an ideal
independent-bit comparison, the illustrative distance distribution would be
Binomial(256,1/2), with mean 128 and standard deviation 8. Distances in this
deterministic neighboring-key experiment are not asserted independent or
binomial.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hmac_avalanche.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/hmac_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::string key =
        "shared-secret-key", message = "transfer $100 to Alice";
    const auto r = dm::algorithms::hmac_key_avalanche(key, message);
    const bool genuine =
        dm::algorithms::hmac_sha256(key, message) == r.baseline;
    const bool tampered =
        dm::algorithms::hmac_sha256(key, "transfer $900 to Mallory") ==
        r.baseline;
    const bool wrong =
        dm::algorithms::hmac_sha256("guessed-key", message) == r.baseline;
    std::print("Genuine equality {}; tampered equality {}; guessed-key equality {}.\n\nComplete key flips " "{}; actual mean {:.9f}; minimum {}; maximum {} of 256 bits.\n",
               genuine, tampered, wrong, r.distances.size(), r.mean, r.minimum,
               r.maximum);
    std::print("\n| exact changed-bit count | frequency |\n| ---: | ---: |\n");
    std::vector<double> bins, counts, index, distance;
    for (std::size_t d = 0; d < r.histogram.size(); ++d) {
        bins.push_back(d);
        counts.push_back(r.histogram[d]);
        if (r.histogram[d])
            std::print("| {} | {} |\n", d, r.histogram[d]);
    }
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.distances.size(); ++i) {
        index.push_back(i);
        distance.push_back(r.distances[i]);
    }
    auto left =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    left.points(index, distance, "actual flips", {37, 99, 235}, 3.).line(
        {0., double(r.distances.size() - 1)}, {128., 128.}, "ideal mean",
        {220, 38, 38}, 1.5).title("Every supplied key bit").x_label(
        "zero-based key-bit index").y_label("tag bits changed").y_limits(
        0, 280);
    right.line(bins, counts, "exact histogram", {37, 99, 235}, 1.5).title(
        "Complete 0..256 histogram").x_label("tag bits changed").y_label(
        "number of flips").x_limits(0, 256).y_limits(0,
                                                     double(
                                                     *std::max_element(
                                                     r.histogram.begin(),
                                                     r.histogram.end())) + 5);
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
    layout.add(left).add(right).size(1250, 620).title("Original transfer fixture: measured key sensitivity").fit_panels().save_svg("build/hmac_avalanche.svg");
    if (!genuine || tampered || wrong ||
        std::accumulate(r.histogram.begin(), r.histogram.end(), std::size_t{0}) !=
        136)
        throw std::runtime_error("original controls");
}
